WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm definitely gonna be the first-star idol!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.610
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.570
So far on Aikatsu Stars!

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:15.950
Mahiru-chan and Aria-chan went on a 
mountain retreat to forge themselves.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:22.160
Both of them put on powerful performances and went way up the Aikatsu Ranking.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.960
But now the Final Tournament is upon us.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.750
We're all striving to become the world's brightest star.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.920
It's time to put my Aikatsu to the test!

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.680
The Aikatsu Ranking! A worldwide event where idols compete for the top spot.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:43.730
Every four years, this Final Tournament is held to determine who the greatest idol is.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:48.820
I will be your host this year! My name is Tsuji! {him repeating his name threw me off}

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.900
Only the idols who battled their way into the 
top four can compete in the Final Tournament.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.070
It's time to announce who made it!

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.580
Sorry I'm late.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.000
I brought Alice-chan too.{why does alice get the honor of watching this in the s4 garden}{Koharu is the white rabbit?}

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.830
I apologize for keeping you.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.380
You got here just in time.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:09.750
This is it.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:10.710
Yeah.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.210
Please...

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:15.090
I'm jittery.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.470
I'm very jittery! {tried to go halfway between nervous and excited}{this is good}

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:21.220
Kirara worked hard! My name's on there for sure!{usually for this kind of stuff you can do math and stuff and know almost exactly what the final standings are though}{I think they only update it periodically, and events are just "a lot" of points}

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.770
Seeing how the results play out will be quite intriguing.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:30.730
Now then, starting from the top!

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.860
In first:

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.870
Venus Ark's Elza Forte-san!

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.120
In second:

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.910
Four Star Academy's Nijino Yume-san!

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:44.000
In third:

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.620
Venus Ark's Kizaki Rei-san!

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:47.750
In fourth:

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.500
Four Star Academy's Kasumi Mahiru-san!

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:56.010
The Aikatsu Ranking Final Tournament will be carried out with these four!

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:35.610
S4 Presents: It's Our Job to Shine.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.150
Yume, Mahiru!

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:41.110
Congrats on making it into the Final Tournament!

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.110
Congratulations!

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.530
Thanks!

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:46.950
But only the winner of the tournament can rightfully be called the world's best idol.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:47.740
Right.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.540
The real fight starts now.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.960
And now that I'm here, I'm in it to win it!

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.710
Osu!

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:03.470
Girls, you'd better not lose to Venus Ark!

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:04.140
Of course.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.340
We won't!

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.930
I'm hyped for the Final Tournament!

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.850
But before that, S4's having a concert.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.190
Our venue will be the Aikatsu Budokan! {I'm going to trust my instict and say we spelled it like this, as it's a known word like Osaka or Tokyo}{we definitely this}

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.980
Wait, you mean <i>the</i> Aikatsu Budokan?!

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.360
The same one where you and the former S4 stood?!

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.650
That's the one.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:30.240
Everyone! I'm expecting to see all your faces over at the Aikatsu Budokan for our concert!

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.000
No one told me about this!

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.750
Well, yeah! That's 'cause I brought it up for the first time just now.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.380
But why this all of a sudden?

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:43.800
Because our iteration of S4 will be graduating soon.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.340
Graduating...

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:48.010
The S4 Selection is approaching too.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:52.140
Yuzu-senpai, you'll be graduating from the middle school, right?

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.270
Yeah, that's why.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:05:00.530
I wanna have a huge show to remember this group with and go out with a bang!

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.440
Yuzu-senpai.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:08.030
We don't have much time. We'll need to rush the preparations for our dresses and program and such.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:11.330
Me and Ako-chan will take care of the dresses.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.790
The rest of you think about what you want to sing.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.420
What songs do we want to sing...

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.920
And what theme should we go with?

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.300
This'll be difficult with the Final Tournament coming up.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.050
We have a lot to do.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:31.060
Should I make a list of all the songs you've done so far?

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.310
That should make it easier to decide.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.770
Thanks, but...

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:37.310
Rola, are you okay?

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:42.070
Oh, you mean how I didn't make the Final Tournament?

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:48.570
I didn't get any points from the Amazing Idol Fes, 
so I already knew it was a long shot.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:52.330
This is just the level I'm at now.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:53.450
Rola...

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:55.330
I'm fine!

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:59.580
I wouldn't be much of a Song Class admin if I let this get me down.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:03.090
I need to go and give a lesson to Song Class.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.300
I'll be back later with that list.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.220
Thanks. Good luck.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:08.010
Yep!

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.550
See you later.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.690
There's no way she's okay.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:21.020
I'm sure it's eating at her. {I want to use a synonym at least once}{true synonyms are a myth}

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.070
For every winner, there's a loser.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:27.190
Aikatsu is unforgiving.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.150
Yeah...

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.120
It's freezing!

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.240
The temperature really dropped today. {and then this point is dropped. I'm inclined to think this scene was added because of all the snowfall in Japan this year}

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.620
Yuzu-senpai is taking her sweet time.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:40.000
Sorry I'm late!

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:42.750
I was bringing guests!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:44.460
Hi!

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:45.460
Hey.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:46.670
Hime-senpai!

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.010
Tsubasa-senpai?

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:49.090
Onee-chan?!

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.840
Mahiru!

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.430
It's been so long!

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:54.470
Onee-chan, when did you get back?

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:55.970
Just now.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:59.600
Did you come to watch the Final Tournament?

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.940
Or is it for the S4 concert we're having?

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:02.860
Neither.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.610
Then why?

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.070
Here's a hint: what's this?

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:17.540
I was kicked out of Venus Ark, and couldn't even make the Final Tournament.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:21.000
Maybe I'm not suited to be an idol after all...

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.710
Is that a crying girl I spy?

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.750
Crying all by herself...

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.050
Roar!

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.440
I saw that!

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.980
You definitely just sighed!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.780
Okay, girls!

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.490
Today's February 3rd.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.780
It's Setsubun!

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:56.160
Let's hold an Aikatsu bean throwing!

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:57.790
We're Demon4! {amazingly, demon is the exact right word for this scene}{zing zing zing zing amazing}

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.660
S-So adorable...

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:03.290
I've never seen such pretty demons in my life! {RIP Ran}

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:05.080
What is all this?

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.880
This is "bean throwing".

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.880
A Japanese tradition in which we throw beans in order to cleanse evil.{I wonder if RF5 is ever going to}

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.050
I see...

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:14.640
Everyone, do you have your beans?

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:16.510
Okay, Sakuraba!

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:17.680
Y-Yes?

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.100
Throw your beans at us! {subtext...}{phrasing...}

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.850
N-No way! Throwing beans at you would be—

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.190
You can't do it?

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.610
Isn't that the reason you lost?

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:28.690
Huh?

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.110
"I can't throw beans at my senpai."

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.740
"I can't beat Elza Forte."

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:37.370
Don't you think that instinct is working against your Aikatsu?

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:38.740
Th-That's not...

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:40.290
It's true, isn't it?

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:45.120
You try to hide your frustration behind a forced smile, all the while sighing to yourself in private.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.880
If you keep up that facade and try to deceive yourself, it'll only encourage your demons.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:51.800
My demons?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.800
Your inner demons, the weaknesses in your heart.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.930
The more you try to conceal them, the bigger they grow.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:04.560
Let's drive those demons out by shouting our feelings and throwing beans!

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.560
Come on!

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.070
Sakuraba! Scream out those emotions you've been bottling up!

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.320
Shout!

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:20.580
I'm mad that I lost! I'm so frustrated it hurts!

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:25.330
I knew that I'd probably lose, 
but I always thought I had a chance!

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:29.080
I really wanted to be in the Final Tournament!

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.340
Rola!

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:33.840
Enough of the person would could only sigh to herself!

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.260
Get out!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:39.050
Demons out!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.390
Good! Keep going!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.060
I won't let this be the end!

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:50.110
Fortune in!

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:51.860
That's it!

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:53.690
How's it feel, Sakuraba?

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:55.240
What?

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.860
Did you get your inner demons out?

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:00.240
Yes! Thank you so much!

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:04.160
Good, good! Next up, it's Alice-chan's turn!

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.410
Okay.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:11.170
I'm ashamed as well. I even promised I would become an idol who could match Elza-san! {ep 60}

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:15.170
But I won't give up! Enough of being a crybaby!

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:17.380
Demons out!

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.720
Good, good!

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.550
Next, Koharu-chan!

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:27.180
Enough of the weakling who thinks she has no talent every time designing clothes doesn't go smoothly!

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:28.480
Demons out!

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:30.810
Yes, that's good!

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.820
Go on, Mahiru!

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:38.950
Sometimes I get so worked up that I forget to enjoy doing Aikatsu.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.610
Enough of being stubborn!

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.320
Demons out!

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:44.370
Okay!

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.620
It is as a certain artist once said: {I guess Narita didn't get the memo that they were citing sources}

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.500
"One's worst enemy is oneself."

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:55.420
While we are our own demons, we are also the ones to call fortune to ourselves.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.260
There's our proverb!

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.380
I have but one wish.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:03.180
That is to Aikatsu in a healthy body!

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:04.810
Fortune in!

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:10.190
You did great, Lilienne!

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:13.190
I'm supposed to only have eyes for Subaru-kyun...

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.480
Only for him...

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:21.450
Kira Kanata, you jerk!

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:24.700
Miss!

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:30.410
Okay, let's drive our demons out!

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.960
Please let us continue!

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.710
They appear to be having fun.

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:42.180
They're drawing out all of the feelings that Nijino's group has been suppressing.

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:46.100
It looks like the Shiratori team's plan worked out.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:51.560
There's no need for us teachers to step in.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:52.390
Yes.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:56.230
Okay, we're done!

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.190
Thank you very much!

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:01.320
How do you all feel? 
Did you get your demons out?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:02.070
Yes!

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:04.370
I haven't vented this much in a long time.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:05.870
I had so much fun.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.330
Me too!

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.200
Yeah, I've decided.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:14.540
Yuzu-senpai, I want to sing Episode Solo for our Aikatsu Budokan concert.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.790
Why's that?

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.630
It came to me while listening to everyone's feelings.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:22.930
Each idol has her own episode, her own story to tell.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:25.760
Most of them may be happy and fun,

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:29.560
but there painful times when we cry tears of frustration too.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:34.560
My Aikatsu started when I met everyone here at Four Star.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:39.150
My story is woven from each and every day we worked hard together.{you can either match the scene changes or the voice lines, I chose the voice lines (it was overlapping before)}{that's because I ran TPP after TL, not sure why my overlap script didn't catch this}

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:43.070
Without everyone, my story wouldn't be the same as it is today.

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.660
Because of everyone, I've grown into who I am today.

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:49.160
After all, you can't write a story alone.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:56.170
That's why I want to sing it while 
hugging everyone's emotions tight. {there are multiple reasons, one of which may not have to do with this series}

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:58.040
Yume...

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:02.840
Episode Solo is the best song for that.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:07.640
But wasn't that the song sung by 
Onee-chan and Hime-senpai's S4?

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:08.430
Yeah.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:11.060
We sang it when I was in S4 too.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:11.810
Huh?

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:14.770
Anna-sensei!

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:18.900
As did the S4 before us, and the one before them, right?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.610
Exactly!

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:28.280
Episode Solo is passed down from one generation of S4 to the next, and rearranged each time to fit its members.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:32.120
I think it's the perfect song for your Aikatsu Budokan show.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.460
Yume-chan, nice choice!

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:37.290
I'm glad, and thank you!

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.100
Aria, you were very close.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.180
I'm very upset.

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:58.350
But that proves I was serious.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:03.980
Next time, I'll work even harder so I can end up happy.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.400
Good. That's the spirit.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:10.280
Now if only Kirara could feel that way as well.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:16.120
Today's steak was made from Maesawa Beef.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.170
How are the others?

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:21.630
Kirara-sama has locked herself in her room.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.960
She had no appetite this morning either.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:31.760
I lost...

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:39.270
I wanted to win the Final Tournament and make Elza-sama reconsider, but now I can't!

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:44.270
Kirara, open the door.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:46.030
Elza-sama!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.650
Open it now.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.530
Caroline!

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.050
There is a proper way to eat steak.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:16.430
No matter how high quality the beef, it all goes to waste if not enjoyed while sizzling hot.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:21.770
Come quickly, before it cools.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:24.730
O-Okay!

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:28.690
Enjoy.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.160
I lost, so I have no right to eat this.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.200
You cannot Aikatsu well on an empty stomach.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:38.040
That goes double if you intend to make your way back up.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.120
Elza-sama...

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.220
It's good.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.140
Sebastian, prepare a second steak for Kirara.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.600
At once.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:07.610
I'll eat! I'll eat lots of steak and make my way back up!

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:14.360
Elza, thank you.

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.540
So this is the Aikatsu Budokan stage!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:27.750
It's so big!

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:29.880
Yeah, it's massive.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:33.760
I-I'm not the slightest bit nervous. You're the same, right Yume?

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.640
Yume?

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:40.390
I was sitting up there two years ago.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.390
Huh?

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:45.850
That's where I first saw Hime-senpai and S4 perform.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:50.360
Hime-senpai was dazzlingly bright and radiant.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:55.910
Seeing that performance inspired me to try to get into S4 and shine just like her.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:00.080
That was when my dream was born.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:04.710
The story of the idol Nijino Yume got its start right here.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.830
Now it's your turn, Yume-chan.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:14.260
Fill up this stage with sparkles and make the whole audience's stories glimmer with your brilliance!

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:17.050
We'll help you make this into an unforgettable scene.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:17.720
Yeah!

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:21.640
All right! I'm gonna shine my heart out!

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.230
Yeah!

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:42.490
We are stars.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:45.250
The Four Stars that light up the Aikatsu world.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:48.500
Tirelessly serving as shining beacons in the sky.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.750
The radiance of S4 is...

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:51.800
Eternal!

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:53.060
Everyone, the wait is over.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:58.570
It's time for a press conference with the Final Tournament contestants.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:05.820
Now then, contestants. Please give us a few words on your thoughts regarding the Final Tournament.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.660
I am perfect.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:10.830
Victory is inevitable.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:14.080
I will fight with all my might and win.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.330
Everything is for Elza!

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:23.840
I will strive to win for both myself and for every single person who supports me.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:26.970
Finishing us up is Nijino Yume-san.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.720
It's my dream...

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:32.350
...to become the world's greatest idol!

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:35.480
Then like the others, you're gunning for first?

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:37.650
That's one of my goals.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:41.110
But more importantly, I want everyone watching,

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:45.900
as well as Elza-san and the others performing,

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:47.910
to shine together with me.

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:52.660
You're naive, Yume Nijino.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:55.410
A competition is meaningless unless you win.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:57.460
There's no "together" about it.

00:21:58.210 --> 00:21:59.920
I believe I can do it.

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:05.920
Elza-san, let's both shine as brightly as we can!

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:08.510
Show me what you've got.

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:09.930
I'll do my best!

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:12.100
Let's fight to the best of our ability.

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:14.560
Of course. Bring it on.

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:19.060
Now, which of these four will rise to become the top idol?

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:24.280
The curtains are rising on the 
Aikatsu Ranking Final Tournament!

00:23:55.780 --> 00:24:01.160
It was like a dream to sing the song passed down through S4 generations in such a lovely dress.

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:05.420
Ever since you crossed the Aikatsu start line that day, you've been running at full speed.

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:08.880
I'll speed ahead as the world's greatest idol!

00:24:10.970 --> 00:24:12.630
It's an emergency!

00:24:12.630 --> 00:24:15.050
Everyone says they're through with lessons!

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:17.390
I want to protect Venus Ark!

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:18.890
For Elza!

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:20.430
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:21.980
Sword of Light.{also part of the subtitle of the first fire emblem game}

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:24.230
Become the first-star idol!
